# CODEOWNERS — who must review changes to which part of the repo.
#
# How it works
#   - GitHub requests a review from the owners of every file a PR touches.
#   - With "Require review from Code Owners" enabled on the `main` branch
#     protection rule, a PR cannot merge until an owner of each touched path
#     approves. See docs/CODEOWNERS.md for the review rules and how to change
#     ownership.
#   - The LAST matching pattern wins. Keep the catch-all first and the most
#     specific (highest-risk) paths last.
#   - Owners must be users or teams with write access to this repository.
#
# Validated by scripts/codeowners.test.mjs (syntax, no stale patterns, every
# top-level directory owned, high-risk paths resolve as intended) and by the
# GitHub CODEOWNERS errors API in the CI tooling job.

